--
N5008 [dcl.fct]/5: a parameter of function type is adjusted to a pointer to
function, so `typedef int F(int());' declares F as int(int (*)()), the type
of cb.  The front end took the parameter `int()' as int: the parser read
`()' as a parenthesized empty declarator.  N5008 [dcl.ambig.res]/3: in a
parameter declarator, `(' followed by `)', `...' or a type-specifier starts
a parameter list (Parser::rDeclarator).  test_type_name_in_parentheses.desc:
the standard's Example 3 (`int(C)' with C a class).  Failed on bin53.  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
